# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
# A production build written beside a running dev server, for measuring the
# performance budgets (NEXT_DIST_DIR in next.config.ts). It must be ignored:
# Tailwind v4 scans the project for class names and skips whatever git
# ignores, so while this directory was not listed it read the minified build
# output, found mangled strings that look like class names, and emitted CSS
# that would not parse — every page of the dev server answered 500.
/.next-measure/
# Any build made to MEASURE or VERIFY, never the one that is served. A build
# directory left untracked is also a directory Tailwind will scan: the first
# time this was forgotten it read minified CSS out of the output, produced an
# unparseable stylesheet, and every page in the dev server answered 500.
/.next-verify/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

uploads/
*.db

# security: local database dumps
# vendored reference template (not part of the app)
# scratch files

# security: local database dumps
backups/
# vendored reference template (not part of the app)
واجهة/
# scratch files
tmp*.cjs

# Fonts licensed for this machine only.
#
# thmanyah, Boutros and the rest permit use on your own devices and forbid
# putting the file anywhere a third party can fetch it. This repository is
# pushed to GitHub, so a font committed here is a font published — which is
# the exact thing those licences prohibit. They stay out of git, and the
# route that serves them refuses to exist in a production build.
/fonts-local/

# zaki-ui's shippable folder is built, never edited.
#
# Every file in it is produced by `scripts/build-dist.mjs` from sources that
# ARE tracked, and the package's tests rebuild it and check its contents on
# every run. Committing it would double the fonts in the repository, churn
# a 260 KB zip on each build, and — the real cost — let a stale dist survive
# a source fix while looking correct.
packages/zaki-ui/dist/
